  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span>Please refer to the </span><a href='https://geoportal.gov.mb.ca:443/maps/manitoba-game-hunting-areas/about' target='_blank' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>Manitoba Game Hunting Areas dataset</span></a><span>. </span></p><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span /></p><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span>Game Hunting Areas (GHAs) are defined under the </span><a href='https://web2.gov.mb.ca:443/laws/regs/current/_pdf-regs.php?reg=220/86' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>Hunting Areas and Zones Regulation </span></a><span>(220/86) of </span><a href='https://web2.gov.mb.ca:443/laws/statutes/ccsm/w130e.php' style='text-decoration:underline;' rel='nofollow ugc'><span>The Wildlife Act </span></a><span>(CCSM c. W130). Game Hunting Areas are used to support boundaries for species specific hunting seasons, harvest allocations, bag limits and associated regulations. Refer to the Hunting Areas and Zones Regulation for GHA boundary descriptions.</span></p><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span /></p><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span /></p><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span style='text-decoration:underline;'>Fields Included </span><span>(</span><span style='font-weight:bold;'>Alias </span><span>(Field Name): Field description)</span></p><ul><li><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>OBJECTID </span><span>(OBJECTID): </span><span>s</span><span>equential unique whole numbers that are automatically generated</span></p></li><li><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>GHA </span><span>(GHA): </span><span>the n</span><span>umber assigned to each Game Hunting Area</span></p></li><li><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>Shape_Length </span><span>(Shape_Length): </span><span>the l</span><span>ength of </span><span>the </span><span>feature in internal units</span></p></li><li><p><span style='font-weight:bold;'>Shape_Area </span><span>(Shape_Area): </span><span>a</span><span>rea of</span><span> the</span><span> feature in internal units squared</span></p></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 0 0;'><span /></p></div></div></div>"
